WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.700
Why.

2
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.700
In many agencies today, nothing
connects HR to identity.

3
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:09.219
Accounts, access and credentials
are created and removed by ticket,

4
00:00:09.219 --> 00:00:10.913
and that costs three ways.

5
00:00:10.913 --> 00:00:12.749
Access outlives the job.

6
00:00:12.749 --> 00:00:16.888
When someone leaves or changes
roles, removal waits for a ticket.

7
00:00:16.888 --> 00:00:21.590
Yet the federal PIV standard, FIPS
201-3, requires a card that can't

8
00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.737
be collected to be terminated within
eighteen hours of notification.

9
00:00:26.737 --> 00:00:29.676
A ticket-driven process
struggles to meet that.

10
00:00:29.676 --> 00:00:32.635
Records drift: the phone
book, the manager and the

11
00:00:32.635 --> 00:00:36.113
approval routing are wrong
until someone files a ticket.

12
00:00:36.113 --> 00:00:39.674
And every joiner, mover and
leaver is help-desk work.

13
00:00:39.674 --> 00:00:42.125
Zero Trust makes the gap visible.

14
00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:44.913
A token proves
cryptographically who signed it.

15
00:00:44.913 --> 00:00:48.688
It can't prove the claim is true:
that the person still works here,

16
00:00:48.688 --> 00:00:51.809
still holds the position
the access was granted for,

17
00:00:51.809 --> 00:00:54.713
still reports to the
supervisor who approved it.

18
00:00:54.713 --> 00:00:57.737
Those are workforce facts,
and they live in HR.

19
00:00:57.737 --> 00:01:02.675
If we do nothing, HR moves to Core
HCM, identity moves to Entra ID,

20
00:01:02.675 --> 00:01:07.680
and we rebuild the same manual
process twice, on new platforms.
